## Document: /products/stocks/common-definition

URL: /en/docs/products/stocks/common-definition


# Common Definition

This page lists every enum value accepted or returned by Stocks Trading endpoints.

**Global rule:** all enum string values are **UPPERCASE** on both request and response.

## side

Used on `/order/place` (request), `/order/history` filter (request), and on every order / trade row
(response).

| Value  | Description |
| ------ | ----------- |
| `BUY`  | Buy side    |
| `SELL` | Sell side   |

## orderType

Used on `/order/place` (request), `/order/history` filter (request), and on every order / trade row
(response).

| Value    | Description  |
| -------- | ------------ |
| `MARKET` | Market order |
| `LIMIT`  | Limit order  |

## timeInForce

Used on `/order/place` (request). Optional; defaults to `DAY`.

| Value | Description                                                                                                                           |
| ----- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `DAY` | Good until end of the trading day (default)                                                                                           |
| `GTC` | Good-til-cancelled. Only supported on `LIMIT` orders. Fractional GTC orders must be placed with `tradingSession = EXTENDED` or `24H`. |

## tradingSession / session

Used on `/order/place` (request) as `tradingSession`; returned on order / trade rows as `session`.
Required for `LIMIT`, forbidden for `MARKET`.

| Value      | Description                                                            |
| ---------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| `RTH`      | Regular Trading Hours (09:30–16:00 ET) only                            |
| `EXTENDED` | Pre-Market + RTH + Post-Market (04:00–20:00 ET)                        |
| `24H`      | Overnight + Pre-Market + RTH + Post-Market (20:00 → next-day 20:00 ET) |

## walletType

Used on `/order/place` (request, BUY side only). Optional; defaults to `CARD`. SELL orders always
settle against `CARD` regardless of what is passed.

| Value  | Description              |
| ------ | ------------------------ |
| `CARD` | Funding wallet (default) |
| `MAIN` | Spot wallet              |

## orderStatus (filter)

Used on `/order/history` as a comma-separated multi-value filter. Accepts only these terminal-status
values; in-flight statuses (`NEW`, `ACCEPTED`) are not valid filter inputs.

| Value              | Description      |
| ------------------ | ---------------- |
| `FILLED`           | Fully filled     |
| `PARTIALLY_FILLED` | Partially filled |
| `CANCELED`         | Canceled         |
| `EXPIRED`          | Expired          |
| `REJECTED`         | Rejected         |

## status (order / trade response)

Returned on each order / trade row. Covers both in-flight and terminal states.

| Value              | Description                                        |
| ------------------ | -------------------------------------------------- |
| `NEW`              | Accepted locally, pending upstream acknowledgement |
| `ACCEPTED`         | Accepted by upstream broker                        |
| `PARTIALLY_FILLED` | Partially filled                                   |
| `FILLED`           | Fully filled                                       |
| `CANCELED`         | Canceled                                           |
| `EXPIRED`          | Expired (end-of-day close for `DAY` orders, etc.)  |
| `REJECTED`         | Rejected                                           |

> **Note:** The `status` field on the **Place Order** response (`/order/place`) and on the **Cancel
> Order** response (`/order/cancel`) is a separate acknowledgement code, not an order lifecycle
> status. It only carries `S` (accepted) or `F` (failed).

## tradability (exchange info)

Returned on `/market/exchangeInfo` → `symbols[].tradability`. Indicates which trading direction is
currently allowed for a symbol.

| Value      | Description                                       |
| ---------- | ------------------------------------------------- |
| `BUY_SELL` | Both buying and selling are allowed.              |
| `BUY`      | Only buying is allowed (new long positions only). |
| `SELL`     | Only selling is allowed (close-only).             |
| `NONE`     | No trading allowed (halted / suspended).          |

## convertType (tokenized)

Used on `/tokenized/convert-status` (request) and returned in `/tokenized/history` and
`/tokenized/convert-status` responses.

| Value    | Description                                             |
| -------- | ------------------------------------------------------- |
| `MINT`   | Mint tokenized asset from an underlying equity holding. |
| `REDEEM` | Redeem tokenized asset back into the underlying equity. |

## status (tokenized convert response)

Returned on `/tokenized/mint`, `/tokenized/redeem`, `/tokenized/convert-status`, and each row of
`/tokenized/history`. This is a **separate status code from the order lifecycle `status`** — mint /
redeem is an async convert flow with its own three-state machine.

| Value | Description                   |
| ----- | ----------------------------- |
| `P`   | Processing (async in flight). |
| `S`   | Success (convert completed).  |
| `F`   | Failed.                       |



---

## Document: /products/stocks/change-log

URL: /en/docs/products/stocks/change-log


# change log

the latest update: 2026-08-12

## 2026-08-12

### Deprecated response fields removed

- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/trade/history` — removed `fee` from `rows`.
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/order/detail` — removed `fee` from `trades`; top-level `fee` and
  `avgFilledPrice` are now documented as present only when the order has at least one fill.

## 2026-08-10

### New parameter for Equity Order Detail

- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/order/detail` — added `clientOrderId` as an alternative lookup key. Either
  `orderId` or `clientOrderId` must be provided. The response now includes `clientOrderId`.

## 2026-07-30

### Rate limit update

- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/tokenized/redeem` — UID rate limit increased from 50 to **200 requests /
  min**.

## 2026-07-20

### Initial release

Stocks Trading API (`/sapi/v1/equity/*`) goes live with 16 REST endpoints plus the user data and
market-data WebSocket streams.

**Market Data** (MARKET_DATA)

- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/market/exchangeInfo` — exchange trading rules and the list of tradable
  symbols; optional `symbol` filter.
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/market/tokenized-assets` — list of tokenized assets with underlying equity
  symbol and multiplier.
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/market/quote` — latest best bid / ask for a single ticker (5s server-side
  cache).

**Trade** (TRADE)

- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/order/place` — place a stock order. Supports all `LIMIT` / `MARKET` × `BUY`
  / `SELL` combinations, with `timeInForce` and `tradingSession`; optional `tokenize`. Rate limit
  200 requests / min (UID).
- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/order/cancel` — cancel a single order by `orderId`.
- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/order/cancel-all` — cancel all open orders for the caller.

**Trade** (USER_DATA)

- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/order/open-orders` — all unfinished (open) orders for the caller.
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/order/history` — paged order history.
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/order/detail` — single order + execution list.
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/trade/history` — paged per-fill trade history.

**Tokenized** (TRADE)

- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/tokenized/mint` — mint a tokenized asset from underlying equity. Target
  tokenized asset is resolved server-side from `underlyingAsset`. Rate limit 50 requests / min
  (UID).
- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/tokenized/redeem` — redeem a tokenized asset back into the underlying.
  Target underlying is resolved server-side from `tokenizedAsset`. Rate limit 50 requests / min
  (UID).

**Tokenized** (USER_DATA)

- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/tokenized/history` — paged mint / redeem history (cursor pagination).
- `GET /sapi/v1/equity/tokenized/convert-status` — query a single mint / redeem request by
  `issuerRequestId`.

**Account** (TRADE)

- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/account/disclaimer` — sign / acknowledge the US equity disclaimer.

**User Data Streams** (USER_STREAM)

- `POST /sapi/v1/equity/listenKey` — create a new stock user-data-stream `listenKey`, or renew an
  existing one.
- WebSocket `{listenKey}@orderReport` — real-time push of the user's order state transitions
  (open-state updates and terminal notifications).

**WebSocket Streams** (public market data)

- WebSocket `price` — all-symbol latest-price snapshot, pushed every 3 seconds.
- WebSocket `{SYMBOL}@quote` — per-symbol best bid / ask, real-time with 200 ms per-symbol throttle.
- WebSocket `{SYMBOL}@kline_{interval}` — per-symbol candlesticks for `5m` / `1h` / `1d` / `1w` /
  `1M` intervals.
- WebSocket `calendar` — market-phase transitions (`PRE_MARKET` / `MARKET_OPEN` / `POST_MARKET` /
  `OVERNIGHT` / `MARKET_CLOSED`).
- WebSocket `{SYMBOL}@tradingStatus` — per-symbol trading-status events (halts, resumes, SSR, LULD).
- WebSocket `{SYMBOL}@tradability` — per-symbol tradable-direction changes.



