## Document: /products/connect-2.0/authentication-and-signing

URL: /en/docs/products/connect-2.0/authentication-and-signing



# Authentication and Signing

Hosted Ramp & Onchain Payment API requests must include the required request headers and signature.

| Parameter                 | Description                                                                | Mandatory |
| ------------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------- | --------- |
| `Content-Type`            | `application/json`                                                         | Yes       |
| `X-Tesla-ClientId`        | Partner client ID provided by Binance.                                     | Yes       |
| `X-Tesla-SignAccessToken` | Access token provided by Binance.                                          | Yes       |
| `X-Tesla-Signature`       | Signature generated from request body, timestamp, and partner private key. | Yes       |
| `X-Tesla-Timestamp`       | Timestamp in milliseconds.                                                 | Yes       |

## Signing model

The signature is generated by signing the request body and timestamp with the partner private key.
The partner keeps the private key and shares the public key with Binance.



