## Document: /products/connect-2.0/on-ramp-buy-apis/0.typical-flow

URL: /en/docs/products/connect-2.0/on-ramp-buy-apis/0.typical-flow


# On-ramp APIs — Typical Flow

On-ramp APIs allow partners to offer a Binance-powered hosted fiat-to-crypto purchase flow. A user
can start from the partner application, get redirected to the Binance-hosted checkout, complete
payment through supported payment methods, and receive the purchased crypto at the configured
destination.

## When to use On-ramp APIs

Use On-ramp APIs when your application wants to help users acquire crypto through a hosted
Binance-powered purchase flow.

## Core Integration APIs used by this flow

On-ramp APIs use the shared [Core Integration APIs](../core-integration-apis/0.overview.md) for
discovery, quote, order creation, order query, and webhook handling:

- Get Supported Trading Pairs
- Get Supported Crypto Networks
- Get Payment Method List
- Get Estimated Quote
- Create Order Link
- Query Order Details
- Order Status Webhook

## Overview

This document describes the standard cryptocurrency purchase flow using Binance Pay Onchain's
on-ramp service. The sequence diagram below illustrates the interaction between partner systems and
Binance Pay Onchain APIs throughout the purchase process.

## Flow Steps

### 1. Initialize

- Partner frontend renders the buy interface for users
- Backend provides necessary configuration and settings (when applicable)

### 2. Query Options

- Fetch supported blockchain networks for crypto delivery
- Retrieve available trading pairs
- Get supported payment methods
- Return data to the frontend
  - You can be done in parallel. Depending on your UI/UX design, you may choose to call these APIs
    in different sequences.

### 3. Get Quote

- Request real-time price quote for the selected trading pair, payment method and amount
- Display quote information to the user

### 4. Create PreOrder

- Submit pre-order request to Binance Pay Onchain with user's selection
- Receive a redirect URL for payment processing

### 5. Payment

- Redirect user to Binance
- User completes the purchase using their preferred payment method
- Binance processes the transaction

### 6. Confirmation

- Receive webhook notifications for order status updates
- Query order details to confirm final transaction status
- Update user interface with purchase results and crypto delivery details

![buy-flow.png](../images/buy-flow.png)

## Sample Create Order Link payloads

The examples below use [Core Integration APIs > Create Order Link](5.pre-order.md). Replace sample
values with your own order ID, destination wallet address, redirect URLs, asset, network, and
enabled payment methods.

### Example 1 — Fixed fiat amount on-ramp

Use this pattern when the user chooses how much fiat to spend and receives the quoted crypto amount.

```jsonc
{
  "externalOrderId": "ramp-20260709-001",
  "fiatCurrency": "EUR",
  "cryptoCurrency": "USDT",
  "amountType": 1,
  "requestedAmount": "100",
  "payMethodCode": "BUY_CARD",
  "payMethodSubCode": "card",
  "network": "BSC",
  "address": "0xbb4CdB9CBd3AB01bD10BaEBF2De08d9173bc095c",
  "redirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/success",
  "failRedirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/failure",
  "clientType": "web",
  "customization": {
    "AUTO_REDIRECTION": true,
  },
}
```

### Example 2 — Fixed crypto amount on-ramp

Use this pattern when the user chooses the crypto amount they want to receive. The required fiat
amount is determined by quote and checkout.

```jsonc
{
  "externalOrderId": "ramp-20260709-002",
  "fiatCurrency": "EUR",
  "cryptoCurrency": "USDT",
  "amountType": 2,
  "requestedAmount": "50",
  "payMethodCode": "BUY_CARD",
  "payMethodSubCode": "card",
  "network": "BSC",
  "address": "0xbb4CdB9CBd3AB01bD10BaEBF2De08d9173bc095c",
  "redirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/success",
  "failRedirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/failure",
  "customization": {
    "LOCK_ORDER_ATTRIBUTES": [6],
    "AUTO_REDIRECTION": true,
  },
}
```

### Example 3 — Let Binance-hosted checkout show available payment methods

Use this pattern when the partner does not want to preselect a payment method. Binance can show
available payment options based on the user, market, fiat currency, asset, amount, and enabled
configuration.

```jsonc
{
  "externalOrderId": "ramp-20260709-003",
  "fiatCurrency": "EUR",
  "cryptoCurrency": "USDT",
  "amountType": 1,
  "requestedAmount": "100",
  "network": "BSC",
  "address": "0xbb4CdB9CBd3AB01bD10BaEBF2De08d9173bc095c",
  "redirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/success",
  "failRedirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/failure",
  "customization": {
    "AUTO_REDIRECTION": true,
  },
}
```

### Example 4 — P2P payment method selected

Use this pattern when the partner wants to route the user to a P2P-supported on-ramp method where
available and enabled.

```jsonc
{
  "externalOrderId": "ramp-20260709-004",
  "fiatCurrency": "EUR",
  "cryptoCurrency": "USDT",
  "amountType": 1,
  "requestedAmount": "100",
  "payMethodCode": "BUY_P2P",
  "payMethodSubCode": "BANK",
  "network": "BSC",
  "address": "0xbb4CdB9CBd3AB01bD10BaEBF2De08d9173bc095c",
  "redirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/success",
  "failRedirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/failure",
  "customization": {
    "P2P_EXPRESS": true,
    "AUTO_REDIRECTION": true,
  },
}
```

### Example 5 — Locked checkout attributes

Use this pattern when the partner needs the user to complete the checkout using the order attributes
defined by the partner. This is useful when the partner must keep selected order details fixed after
creating the order link.

```jsonc
{
  "externalOrderId": "ramp-20260709-005",
  "fiatCurrency": "EUR",
  "cryptoCurrency": "USDT",
  "amountType": 2,
  "requestedAmount": "100",
  "payMethodCode": "BUY_CARD",
  "payMethodSubCode": "card",
  "network": "BSC",
  "address": "0xbb4CdB9CBd3AB01bD10BaEBF2De08d9173bc095c",
  "redirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/success",
  "failRedirectUrl": "https://partner.example.com/ramp/failure",
  "customization": {
    "LOCK_ORDER_ATTRIBUTES": [6],
    "AUTO_REDIRECTION": true,
  },
}
```

### Mix and match customization

The payloads above are examples of common partner patterns. Partners can combine available request
fields and approved customization keys to match their checkout requirements.

| Partner need                                       | Fields or customization to consider                                                      |
| -------------------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| User spends a fixed fiat amount                    | `amountType: 1`, `requestedAmount`, `fiatCurrency`                                       |
| User receives a fixed crypto amount                | `amountType: 2`, `requestedAmount`, `cryptoCurrency`, optionally `LOCK_ORDER_ATTRIBUTES` |
| Partner wants to preselect payment method          | `payMethodCode`, `payMethodSubCode`                                                      |
| Partner wants Binance to show available choices    | Omit `payMethodCode` and `payMethodSubCode` where supported                              |
| Partner wants to keep selected order details fixed | `LOCK_ORDER_ATTRIBUTES`, if approved and enabled                                         |

> **Important:** The payloads above show request patterns using existing fields. Actual supported
> assets, networks, payment methods, and customization keys depend on partner enablement and should
> be confirmed with Binance before production use.

## Related configuration

Depending on partner eligibility and product setup, On-ramp APIs may be used together with
customized checkout behavior, Smart Convert Top-Up, Buy Any Token / Swap, supported asset
configuration, supported network configuration, and payment method configuration.



---

## Document: /products/connect-2.0/off-ramp-sell-apis/5.get-payment-method-list-v2

URL: /en/docs/products/connect-2.0/off-ramp-sell-apis/5.get-payment-method-list-v2


# Get payment method list v2

```
POST /papi/v2/ramp/connect/sell/payment-method-list
```

### Request Body

| **Field** | **Type** | **Mandatory** | **Remarks**                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                        |
| --------- | -------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| language  | string   | No            | Language code, which determines the multi-language of the content(if any, such as "payment method name") in the response data. If not passed, English is the default. The format is "[LanguageCode](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ISO_639_language_codes)-[RegionCode](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISO_3166-1)", RegionCode is optional. |

### Response Body

##### Data: PaymentMethodV2Object array

| **Field**      | **Type**     | **Remarks**                                                  |
| -------------- | ------------ | ------------------------------------------------------------ |
| fiatCurrency   | string       | Fiat currency                                                |
| paymentMethods | object array | Payment method details. Refer to PaymentMethodV2DetailObject |

##### PaymentMethodV2DetailObject

| **Field**        | **Type** | **Remarks**                                                |
| ---------------- | -------- | ---------------------------------------------------------- |
| payMethodCode    | string   | payment method code                                        |
| payMethodSubCode | string   | payment method sub code                                    |
| paymentMethod    | string   | payment method display name                                |
| p2p              | bool     | Indicate whether the payment method belongs to Binance P2P |

#

### Example

Request Parameters:

```json
{
  "language": "zh-CN"
}
```

Response:

```json
{
  "success": true,
  "code": "000000",
  "message": "success",
  "data": [
    {
      "fiat": "AED",
      "paymentMethods": [
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_APPLE_PAY",
          "channelCode": "APPLE_PAY",
          "paymentMethod": "Apple Pay (VISA)",
          "p2p": false
        },
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_P2P",
          "channelCode": "BANK",
          "paymentMethod": "Bank",
          "p2p": true
        },
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_P2P",
          "channelCode": "Paypal",
          "paymentMethod": "PayPal",
          "p2p": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "fiat": "EUR",
      "paymentMethods": [
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_WALLET",
          "channelCode": "Wallet",
          "paymentMethod": "Spot Wallet",
          "p2p": false
        },
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_CARD",
          "channelCode": "card",
          "paymentMethod": "Card (VISA/Mastercard)",
          "p2p": false
        },
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_P2P",
          "channelCode": "SEPA",
          "paymentMethod": "SEPA (EU) bank transfer",
          "p2p": true
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "fiat": "CNY",
      "paymentMethods": [
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_P2P",
          "channelCode": "ALIPAY",
          "paymentMethod": "Alipay English",
          "p2p": true
        },
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_P2P",
          "channelCode": "BANK",
          "paymentMethod": "Bank",
          "p2p": true
        },
        {
          "paymentMethodCode": "SELL_P2P",
          "channelCode": "WECHAT",
          "paymentMethod": "WeChat",
          "p2p": true
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
```

##### About payment method "SELL_WALLET"

"SELL_WALLET" is a special payment method that allows users to sell crypto for fiat currency
balances in their Binance wallets.

For example, in some countries or regions, Binance supports users to deposit and withdraw fiat
currencies (such as euro - EUR) directly. At this time, users can sell crypto for EUR (in Binance
wallet). We call this payment method as "SELL_WALLET".



---

## Document: /products/connect-2.0/off-ramp-sell-apis/4.pre-order

URL: /en/docs/products/connect-2.0/off-ramp-sell-apis/4.pre-order


# Pre order

```
POST /papi/v1/ramp/connect/sell/pre-order
```

### Request Body

| **Field**            | **Type** | **Mandatory** | **Remarks**                                                                                                    |
| -------------------- | -------- | ------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| externalOrderId      | string   | Yes           | The unique order id from the partner side. Supports only letters and numbers.                                  |
| fiatCurrency         | string   | Yes           | fiat currency                                                                                                  |
| cryptoCurrency       | string   | Yes           | crypto currency                                                                                                |
| amountType           | int      | Yes           | Specify whether the requested amount is in fiat:1 or crypto:2                                                  |
| requestedAmount      | string   | Yes           | Requested amount. Fraction is 8                                                                                |
| payMethodCode        | string   | Yes           | The payment method code is from payment method list API                                                        |
| payMethodSubCode     | string   | Yes           | The payment method subcode is from payment method list API                                                     |
| network              | string   | Yes           | crypto network                                                                                                 |
| redirectUrl          | string   | No            | The redirectUrl is for redirecting to your website if order is completed                                       |
| failRedirectUrl      | string   | No            | The redirectUrl is for redirecting to your website if order is failed                                          |
| redirectDeepLink     | string   | No            | The redirectDeepLink is for redirecting to your APP if order is completed                                      |
| failRedirectDeepLink | string   | No            | The failRedirectDeepLink is for redirecting to your APP if order is failed                                     |
| clientIp             | string   | No            | The original client IP                                                                                         |
| clientType           | string   | No            | The original client type: web/mobile                                                                           |
| customization        | object   | No            | Customization settings for the current order. Please refer to "[Customization](../basics/9.customization.md)". |

### Response Body

| **Field**      | **Type**  | **Remarks**                                                                                                                                                                    |
| -------------- | --------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------ |
| link           | string    | The landing page link of Binance Pay Onchain. For information on how to use it, please refer to "[Landing page and redirection](../basics/8.landing-page-and-redirection.md)". |
| linkExpireTime | timestamp | The expiration time of link                                                                                                                                                    |

#

### Example

Request Parameters:

```json
{
