## Document: /products/connect-2.0/basics/6.apply-developer-account

URL: /en/docs/products/connect-2.0/basics/6.apply-developer-account


# How to apply partner developer account

If you are a partner (client) who wants to integrate Binance Pay Onchain’s Open API. Please contact
Binance Pay Onchain team and provide the following items:

- [Public key](3.request-signing.md) for API requests (private key kept by the partner/client
  safely);
- IP addresses used to config whitelist;
- Webhook callback url;
- The domains of the URL/Universal Link that you will pass to the `redirectUrl` and
  `failRedirectUrl` parameters of the pre-order API, as well as the schema of the Deeplink of the
  `redirectDeepLink` and `failRedirectDeepLink` parameters. Which are used to config whitelist for
  redirecting users back to your platform when on/off ramp completed;
- A logo image in format of 80 x 80 pixel png, which will be displayed on the Binance Pay Onchain
  page.

Once Binance Pay Onchain receives these items and completes the configuration, Binance Pay Onchain
will provide the following items to the partner (client):

- Client id;
- Sign access token;
- Public key and partner code for webhook (private key kept by Binance Pay Onchain safely);

Then the partner (client) will be able to call all Open APIs.

> \*_Regarding to different environments, please refer to
> “[Environments and API base URLs](4.base-urls.md)”. It‘s recommended to start with the QA
> environment first._



